If $X ~ N(mu, sigma^2)$ and $Y ~ N(nu, tau^2)$ are independent, their moment generating functions multiply:
$
  EE[ee^(theta (X + Y))] = exp(mu theta + (theta^2 sigma^2)/2) exp(nu theta + (theta^2 tau^2)/2) = exp((mu + nu) theta + (theta^2 (sigma^2 + tau^2))/2),
$
so $X + Y ~ N(mu + nu, sigma^2 + tau^2)$: sums of independent normal random variables are normal.
